                    <div class="article-container-text">
                        <h2 class="article-headline">About The Beltway Times</h2>
                        <p class="article-excerpt">
                            Every story begins with something that actually happened. Then we treat it like breaking news on a comedy network for a country that is both hilarious and sad.
                        </p>
                        <div class="my-3">

                            <h3 class="text-red mb-2">Editorial Values</h3>
                            <ul class="lh-1-6 mb-3">
                                <li>Report truth with hypocracy.</li>
                                <li>Punch up at power, privilege, and performative outrage.</li>
                                <li>Make the news as hilarious as the politics.</li>
                            </ul>

                            <h3 class="text-red mb-2">Reader’s Guide</h3>
                            <ul class="lh-1-6 mb-3">
                                <li>If it reads like it could be fake but rings oddly true, that’s the point.</li>
                                <li>If you’re unsure whether to laugh or sigh—you’re doing it correctly.</li>                            </ul>

                            <div class="about-disclaimer my-3">
                                <p class="m-0 italic text-gray">
                                    LEGAL DISCLAIMER: We exaggerate and dramatize-but we do not fabricate events. All commentary is for entertainment purposes and rooted in things that genuinely occurred, even if they sound like they shouldn’t have.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>
            </div>
            </article>
